Here's a comprehensive prompt for the frontend developer to implement the new API endpoints and features:
Frontend Implementation Prompt: Smart-Tutor API Updates
Overview
The backend has been updated with several new endpoints and features. This prompt explains how to integrate them into the frontend.
1. Authentication - Portal Field
Login with Portal Selection
Endpoint: `POST /auth/login`
New Field: `portal` (optional, defaults to 'PARENT')
// Login request body{  email: string,  password: string,  portal?: 'PARENT' | 'TUTOR' | 'ADMIN'}
Implementation:
- Add a portal selector/dropdown on the login page with three options: Parent, Tutor, Admin
- The portal field determines which login rate limit applies and validates the user's role
- If the user's role doesn't match the selected portal, the API returns 401 "Invalid credentials" (same as wrong password - no role leak)
- Admin portal has stricter rate limiting (5 requests per 15 minutes vs 7 for others)
- PENDING_VETTING tutors can now log in through the TUTOR portal
Error Handling:
- 401 "Invalid credentials" - wrong password OR portal mismatch
- 403 "Please verify your email first" - unverified account
- 403 "Account is not active" - suspended/rejected account
- 403 "Your account is pending admin approval" - only if trying to login as non-TUTOR portal
UI Changes Needed:
- Add portal selection UI (radio buttons, tabs, or dropdown)
- Update login form to include portal field
- Consider separate login pages/routes for each portal (e.g., `/login/parent`, `/login/tutor`, `/login/admin`)
2. Badge Counts - All Roles
GET /badge-counts
Endpoint: `GET /badge-counts`
Auth: Required (any role)
Response varies by role:
For PARENT:
{  "unreadNotifications": {    "ENROLLMENTS": number,    "PAYMENTS": number,    "SESSIONS": number,    "MESSAGES": number,    "GRADES": number,    "ASSIGNMENTS": number,    "QUIZZES": number,    "PROGRESS": number,    "SCHEDULE": number,    "PRICING": number,    "COMPLAINTS": number,    "OTHER": number  },  "unpaidEnrollments": number,  "upcomingSessions24h": number,  "unreadMessages": number}
For TUTOR:
{  "unreadNotifications": {    "SESSIONS": number,    "MESSAGES": number,    "ASSIGNMENTS": number,    "GRADES": number,    "COMPLAINTS": number,    "OTHER": number  },  "sessionsNeedingScheduling": number,  "classesWithin24h": number,  "draftOrRejectedGrades": number,  "unmarkedAttendance": number,  "unreadMessages": number,  "submissionsToScore": number}
For STUDENT:
{  "unreadNotifications": {    "ASSIGNMENTS": number,    "SESSIONS": number,    "MESSAGES": number,    "GRADES": number,    "QUIZZES": number,    "OTHER": number  },  "pendingAssignments": number,  "classesWithin24h": number}
For ADMIN:
{  "unreadNotifications": { /* all categories */ },  "pendingTutorApplications": number,  "pendingGrades": number,  "openComplaints": number,  "unmatchedPaidEnrollments": number,  "pendingChangeRequests": number,  "unscheduledWithin24h": number,  "failedPayments": number,  "outstandingEnrollments": number,  "unreadMessages": number,  "attendanceUnmarkedSessions": number}
Implementation:
- Create a unified badge count component that works for all roles
- Use role-specific badge counts to show notifications in the UI
- Example: Show a badge on "Messages" icon with `unreadMessages` count
- Show badge on "Assignments" with `pendingAssignments` (student) or `submissionsToScore` (tutor)
- Show badge on "Grades" with `pendingGrades` (admin) or `draftOrRejectedGrades` (tutor)
- For admin, show badge on various admin sections based on counts
Existing Admin Endpoint:
- `GET /admin/badge-counts` still exists and is admin-only
- It now includes `attendanceUnmarkedSessions` field
- You can use either endpoint for admin users
3. Salary Management (Admin Only)
PATCH /admin/tutors/:id/salary
Endpoint: `PATCH /admin/tutors/:id/salary`
Auth: Required (ADMIN)
Request Body:
{  monthlySalaryNGN: number, // positive integer, required  reason?: string}
Response (200):
{  "id": "uuid",  "monthlySalaryNGN": number,  "oldValue": number | null,  "newValue": number,  "changedBy": "uuid",  "reason": "string | null",  "createdAt": "ISO date"}
Implementation:
- Add salary edit functionality in admin tutor detail page
- Show current salary (if set) or "Not Set" message
- Form should validate: positive number required, null/zero rejected
- Show success message after update
- Display salary history in a separate section/tab
GET /admin/tutors/:id/salary-history
Endpoint: `GET /admin/tutors/:id/salary-history`
Auth: Required (ADMIN)
Response (200):
[  {    "id": "uuid",    "tutorId": "uuid",    "oldValue": number | null,    "newValue": number,    "changedBy": "uuid",    "reason": "string | null",    "createdAt": "ISO date"  }]
Implementation:
- Display salary change history in a table or timeline
- Show old value, new value, who changed it, reason, and timestamp
- Sort by createdAt descending (most recent first)
GET /tutor-profile (Updated)
Endpoint: `GET /tutor-profile`
Auth: Required (TUTOR, APPROVED)
Response now includes:
{  "id": "uuid",  "userId": "uuid",  "subjects": ["Mathematics", "Physics"],  "bio": "string",  "credentialsUrl": "string",  "monthlySalaryNGN": 50000, // NEW - replaces hourlyRate  "availability": {},  "availabilityStatus": "AVAILABLE",  "maxStudents": null,  "statusNote": null,  "statusUpdatedAt": "ISO date",  "createdAt": "ISO date",  "updatedAt": "ISO date",  "user": { /* user info */ }}
Changes:
- `hourlyRate` field removed
- `monthlySalaryNGN` field added (nullable until admin sets it)
- Display monthly salary in tutor profile page (read-only for tutors)
- Tutors cannot edit their own salary - only admins can
4. Schedule Visibility
GET /tutor/students (Updated)
Endpoint: `GET /tutor/students`
Auth: Required (TUTOR, APPROVED)
Response now includes:
[  {    "student": {      "id": "uuid",      "fullName": "string",      "gradeLevel": "G5_TO_G8",      "school": "string"    },    "enrollment": {      "id": "uuid",      "subjectId": "uuid",      "sessionFrequency": "WEEKLY",      "availableDays": ["MON", "WED", "FRI"],      "preferredStartHour": 14,      "preferredEndHour": 15,      "scheduleTimezone": "Africa/Lagos",      "startDate": "ISO date",      "endDate": "ISO date",      "startTimeUtc": "ISO date",      "status": "ACTIVE",      "nextExpectedClass": {        "id": "uuid",        "scheduledAt": "ISO date",        "status": "SCHEDULED"      },      "sessionsScheduledCount": 5    },    "subject": {      "id": "uuid",      "name": "Mathematics"    }  }]
New Fields:
- `availableDays` - array of days (MON, TUE, WED, THU, FRI, SAT, SUN)
- `preferredStartHour` - preferred start hour (0-23)
- `preferredEndHour` - preferred end hour (0-23)
- `scheduleTimezone` - timezone where hours were entered (e.g., "Africa/Lagos")
- `startTimeUtc` - computed UTC start time
- `nextExpectedClass` - next upcoming session (or null)
- `sessionsScheduledCount` - total number of scheduled sessions
Implementation:
- Update tutor students list to show schedule information
- Display preferred time window in student's timezone
- Show next expected class date/time
- Show count of scheduled sessions
- Consider adding a calendar/schedule view for better visualization
GET /admin/class-schedule (Updated)
Endpoint: `GET /admin/class-schedule`
Auth: Required (ADMIN)
Query Parameters:
mode?: 'sessions' | 'enrollments' (default: 'sessions')tutorId?: uuidsubjectId?: uuidstatus?: 'SCHEDULED' | 'UNSCHEDULED' | 'MISSED' | 'NOT_STARTED' (for enrollments mode)from?: ISO dateto?: ISO datesearch?: stringpage?: numberlimit?: number (max 100)
Mode: sessions (default)
Returns scheduled sessions with participant info.
Mode: enrollments
Returns all active paid enrollments with schedule info:
{  "data": [    {      "id": "uuid",      "student": { "id": "uuid", "fullName": "string" },      "tutor": { "id": "uuid", "fullName": "string" },      "subject": { "id": "uuid", "name": "string" },      "startDate": "ISO date",      "endDate": "ISO date",      "availableDays": ["MON", "WED", "FRI"],      "preferredStartHour": 14,      "preferredEndHour": 15,      "scheduleTimezone": "Africa/Lagos",      "sessionFrequency": "WEEKLY",      "status": "SCHEDULED",      "nextExpectedClass": {        "id": "uuid",        "scheduledAt": "ISO date",        "status": "SCHEDULED"      },      "sessionsScheduledCount": 5    }  ],  "page": 1,  "limit": 20,  "total": 50}
Status Values:
- `SCHEDULED` - has upcoming session
- `UNSCHEDULED` - started but no session scheduled
- `MISSED` - had sessions but none upcoming
- `NOT_STARTED` - future start date
Implementation:
- Add mode toggle (sessions/enrollments) to admin class schedule page
- Add filters for tutorId, subjectId, status, date range, search
- Display enrollment schedule information in a table
- Show status badges for different enrollment statuses
- Implement pagination
5. Assignment Submissions and Scoring
GET /assignments/:id/submissions (Updated)
Endpoint: `GET /assignments/:id/submissions`
Auth: Required (TUTOR for own assignments, PARENT for children's assignments)
Response now includes:
[  {    "id": "uuid",    "assignmentId": "uuid",    "studentId": "uuid",    "studentName": "string",    "status": "SUBMITTED | GRADED",    "textAnswer": "string | null",    "attachmentUrl": "string | null",    "attachmentName": "string | null",    "submittedAt": "ISO date",    "feedbackText": "string | null",    "feedbackAttachmentUrl": "string | null",    "feedbackAttachmentName": "string | null",    "gradedAt": "ISO date | null",    "scoredItem": {      "id": "uuid",      "score": number,      "maxScore": number,      "comment": "string",      "scoredAt": "ISO date"    } | null,    "student": {      "id": "uuid",      "fullName": "string",      "user": {        "id": "uuid",        "email": "string"      }    }  }]
New Fields:
- `status` - SUBMITTED or GRADED
- `scoredItem` - scored item details if graded (or null)
Implementation:
- Show submission status (Submitted/Graded) in the list
- Display scored item details if available
- Add visual indicators for graded vs ungraded submissions
POST /tutor/assignments/:id/submissions/:submissionId/score
Endpoint: `POST /tutor/assignments/:id/submissions/:submissionId/score`
Auth: Required (TUTOR, APPROVED)
Request Body:
{  score: number, // non-negative  maxScore?: number, // positive, default 100  comment?: string}
Response (201):
{  "id": "uuid",  "tutorId": "uuid",  "studentId": "uuid",  "enrollmentId": "uuid",  "type": "QUIZ | ASSIGNMENT | CLASSWORK | TEST | HOMEWORK | PROJECT | PARTICIPATION",  "sourceType": "AssignmentSubmission",  "sourceId": "uuid",  "score": number,  "maxScore": number,  "comment": "string",  "scoredAt": "ISO date",  "createdAt": "ISO date",  "updatedAt": "ISO date"}
Implementation:
- Add scoring functionality to tutor assignment submissions view
- Show scoring form when submission status is SUBMITTED
- Display score input, max score input (default 100), and comment field
- After scoring, submission status changes to GRADED
- Show scored item details in the submission view
- Handle error: "Submission has already been scored" (400)
ScoredItem Types:
- QUIZ → QUIZ
- ASSIGNMENT → ASSIGNMENT
- CLASSWORK → CLASSWORK
- TEST → TEST
- HOMEWORK → HOMEWORK
- PROJECT → PROJECT
