This prompt should provide the frontend developer with all the information needed to implement the new API endpoints and features.

Read ENDPOINT.md (source of truth) and FRONTEND_PROGRESS.md. Do not rebuild screens that work; upgrade them. No invented fields: use tolerant adapters in lib/api.ts and note unclear ones in BACKEND_GAPS.md. No tests. Never print secrets. No git push. After each numbered item run `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build`, fix errors, tick FRONTEND_PROGRESS.md, and commit.

1. SEPARATE PORTALS. Public routes: / is the parent landing page; /tutors is a tutor landing page (become a tutor: benefits, how applying works, vetting steps, CTA to /tutor/register); /login is parent login (links to parent register and forgot password); /register is parent register; /tutor/login is tutor login; /tutor/register is tutor register; /admin/login is the admin login: no register link, no forgot-link to public pages, noindex meta, not linked from any public page or footer, plain minimal design with a clear "Administrator sign in" heading; /student-login stays. Each login sends portal: 'PARENT' | 'TUTOR' | 'ADMIN' to POST /auth/login. A wrong-role failure shows the same generic "Invalid credentials" message. Remove the role selector from login forms. The public navbar shows Parent login and Tutor login only (never admin). Route guards: an unauthenticated visit to /admin/* redirects to /admin/login, /tutor/* (except public tutor pages) to /tutor/login, /parent/* to /login, /student/* to /student-login. Logged-in users hitting the wrong area go to their own dashboard. Logout returns to the matching login page. Make the 401, TUTOR_NOT_APPROVED and APPLICATION_REJECTED redirects respect this.
2. SALARY. Remove every hourly rate field and label everywhere. Tutor registration/application: a required "Expected monthly salary (NGN)" field formatted with ₦ and thousand separators, validated per the docs, shown on the review step. Tutor profile: show monthly salary as READ-ONLY with a note "Only the admin can change this." (no edit control, no delete). Admin tutor detail: show the salary, an Edit button (a modal requiring a new positive value and an optional reason, no clear or delete option), the salary history list (old, new, by, reason, date), and a "Salary not set" warning badge when salaryNotSet. Parents and students never see salary.
3. SCHEDULE VISIBILITY. Tutor: in the students list and student detail, show for each enrollment a clear schedule card: Starts (date, with "starts in N days" if in the future), Days of the week (chips), Time (start to end with timezone label and conversion to the tutor's timezone), Next expected class, and a "Create session" button prefilled. The upcoming-classes page groups by day with the same info. Admin: a new "Student schedules" tab on /admin/class-schedule using mode=enrollments: table of every student with tutor, subject, start date, days, time window and timezone, next class, status chip (SCHEDULED, UNSCHEDULED, MISSED, NOT_STARTED), filters (tutor, subject, status, date range, search), pagination. Make start date, days and time prominent on admin enrollment and student detail pages too. Never show parent contact to tutors or prices to tutors and students.
4. SUBMISSIONS AND SCORING. Tutor: on each assignment, a "Submissions" view (GET /tutor/assignments/:id/submissions) listing student, status, text, attachment (authenticated download), submittedAt, with a "Score" action (score, max score, comment) calling the score endpoint; graded submissions show the scored item. In-session tests and classwork use "Add score". Add a short info box in the scored items tab: "Scores are private to you. Combine them into a grade to send to admin." Student: assignment status SUBMITTED or GRADED only, never the score before a grade is approved. Show a clear "Needs scoring" count on the tutor sidebar via badges.
5. ATTENDANCE UX. Tutor: after completing a session, a prompt "Mark attendance" listing the students (present or absent) in the session modal, and a list of sessions with unmarked attendance on the sessions page with a badge. Student and parent: attendance page with the rate and records. Admin: a "Missing attendance" filter on the sessions page.
6. BADGES PER USER. Replace useBadgeCounts so it calls GET /badge-counts for every role (role-aware, own data only) and additionally GET /admin/badge-counts only when the user is ADMIN. Never reuse admin counts for other roles, never cache counts across logins (clear all badge state, SSE connection and cached data on logout or user change). Map badges per role from the documented fields only (tutor: sessionsNeedingScheduling, classesWithin24h, draftOrRejectedGrades, unmarkedAttendance, submissionsToScore, unreadMessages; parent: unpaid enrollments, upcoming within 24h, unread messages, unread by category; student: pending assignments, classes within 24h, unread by category; admin: the existing admin counts plus attendanceUnmarkedSessions). Each badge is a red count (99+ cap, accessible label) next to the sidebar text. Keep NEW pills, bell, sound on live events only, tab title count.
7. Run `npx tsc --noEmit`, `npm run lint` and `npm run build`, fix errors, and report a table of items 1 to 6 (Done, Partial, Not done) with files changed. State that nothing ran against the live backend.